// =============================================================================
// Detection: Member added to a role-holding / PIM-governed group outside PIM
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform  (lab/ - ITDR pack)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   The way around the lab's own zero-standing-privilege design (ADR 0002):
//   roles sit on role-assignable GROUPS (Break-Glass-Admins = standing Global
//   Administrator, Privileged-IAM-Admins, the PIM-Tier* groups, the Azure
//   PIM group), and elevation is a PIM-for-Groups membership ACTIVATION that
//   expires. Anyone who can write group membership directly gets the group's
//   role permanently, with no approval, no expiry and no activation alert
//   (EXCEPT the Azure PIM group - see AZURE PIM GROUP below):
//     "Add member to group" (Core Directory) on one of those groups, NOT
//        written by MS-PIM (PIM activations write it as MS-PIM)    -> Direct
//     "Add member to role in PIM completed (permanent)" on a group
//        (PIM for Groups, an ACTIVE permanent membership)          -> PimPermanentActive
//     "... completed (timebound)" (active, but expires)            -> PimTimeboundActive
//   One "add attacker to Break-Glass-Admins" = Global Administrator that every
//   CA policy excludes; break-glass-signin.kql would only see the attacker's
//   account if it were named bg-admin-NN. This rule is the one that fires.
//
// AZURE PIM GROUP (PIM-Azure-RG-Contributors, modules/pim azure.tf)
//   Different by design: the GROUP is ELIGIBLE for Contributor on the lab RG,
//   and its people are ordinary STANDING members added directly (the module
//   README's POST /groups/<id>/members/$ref). A new member gets no role - only
//   the right to REQUEST an Azure PIM activation, which still needs MFA,
//   justification and PIM-Approvers-Tier0 approval. So an add there is the
//   intended operational path: AssignmentPath "AzurePimEligibleMember",
//   Medium (it still widens who may ask for Tier 0, so it is never silent).
//   The activation itself is in the Azure Activity Log / PIM audit, not here.
//
// SEVERITY (dynamic - the Severity column)
//   High   : any add to Break-Glass-Admins (even by the CI apply identity: IaC
//            only ever needs to create the two bg-admin members, once), any
//            Direct or PimPermanentActive add to a role-HOLDING group not
//            made by the CI apply identity, and anything by an app only
//            NAMED like it (IacNameSpoof).
//   Medium : the CI apply identity (matched by immutable id), a time-bound
//            active PIM membership, or a member added to the Azure PIM group
//            (AzurePimEligibleMember).
//
// WHICH GROUPS
//   PrivilegedGroupIds is rendered by modules/monitoring from module outputs
//   (groups + pim): Break-Glass-Admins, Privileged-IAM-Admins, every PIM tier
//   group, the Azure PIM group, and the PIM approver groups (members approve
//   Tier-0 activations; membership changes only by Terraform PR). Ids,
//   because a display name can be changed by the very admin being detected.
//   Run standalone (empty list), the name fallback below still covers the
//   lab's groups - names are a fallback only.
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   AuditLogs, Category "GroupManagement", LoggedByService "Core Directory"
//   (direct adds) and "PIM" (PIM for Groups). Operation names: Microsoft Learn
//   "audit log activity reference" (Core Directory + PIM sections).
//   verify: on the first lab add, which TargetResources entry is the group
//   (type "Group") and which the member; the query also reads the
//   Group.ObjectID / Group.DisplayName modified properties for that reason.
//
// LICENSE
//   PIM for Groups needs Entra ID P2 / Governance; the detection itself only
//   needs AuditLogs in Log Analytics.
//
// MITRE ATT&CK
//   T1098.003 Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles (through a
//     role-assignable group)
//   T1098.007 Account Manipulation: Additional Local or Domain Groups -
//     closest technique for cloud group membership
//   Tactics: Persistence, PrivilegeEscalation
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - envs/dev adding the two bg-admin accounts to Break-Glass-Admins on the
//     first premium apply: High BY DESIGN, expected exactly twice; record it.
//   - modules/groups / pim adding members the PR shows (Medium via the IaC
//     identity's id).
//   - A PIM-for-Groups ACTIVATION is not this rule (it is MS-PIM-written and
//     appears in pim-activation.kql).
//   - An operator adding a person to PIM-Azure-RG-Contributors: the intended
//     path (Medium, AzurePimEligibleMember). Check it matches a reviewed
//     request and that the person is an adm- account.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   Frequency 5m · Lookback 1h · one alert per row · Severity column ·
//   Entities: Account = ActorUpn / ActorObjectId, IP = ActorIp.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE
//   Notify on every incident; containment card on High (the ACTOR is the
//   subject: whoever can write privileged group membership holds Tier 0).
//   Removing the member is a manual runbook step - the playbook never edits
//   group membership.
// =============================================================================

let LookBack = 1h;
// The CI apply identity, matched on IMMUTABLE ids (service principal object
// id / application client id), never on its display name: anyone who owns or
// administers an app can rename it "gh-oidc-entra-apply (write)", and a
// display-name match would DOWNGRADE that attacker's changes.
// modules/monitoring renders the list from var.iac_principal_ids (envs/
// bootstrap output iac_principal_ids). Committed, it is empty: run as-is,
// nothing counts as IaC - fail closed, severity can only go up.
let IacPrincipalIds = dynamic([]); // @@IAC_PRINCIPAL_IDS@@
let IacDisplayName = "gh-oidc-entra-apply (write)"; // impersonation check ONLY, never trust
// Role-holding / PIM-governed groups by object id (rendered by Terraform).
let PrivilegedGroupIds = dynamic(["aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa"]); // @@PRIVILEGED_GROUP_IDS@@
let BreakGlassGroupIds = dynamic([]); // @@BREAK_GLASS_GROUP_IDS@@
// PIM-Azure-RG-Contributors by object id (rendered by Terraform): standing
// members are its design (the group is ELIGIBLE for the Azure role).
let AzurePimGroupIds = dynamic([]); // @@AZURE_PIM_GROUP_IDS@@
// Name fallback (standalone runs only; renameable, so never the only check).
let PrivilegedGroupNames = dynamic(["Break-Glass-Admins", "Privileged-IAM-Admins", "PIM-Azure-RG-Contributors"]);
let PimGroupOps = dynamic(["Add member to role in PIM completed (permanent)",
                           "Add member to role in PIM completed (timebound)"]);
AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack)
| where Category == "GroupManagement"
| where Result =~ "success"
| where (OperationName =~ "Add member to group" and Identity !in ("MS-PIM", "MS-PIM-Fairfax"))
     or (LoggedByService =~ "PIM" and OperationName in~ (PimGroupOps))
| extend AssignmentPath = case(
    OperationName =~ "Add member to role in PIM completed (permanent)", "PimPermanentActive",
    OperationName =~ "Add member to role in PIM completed (timebound)", "PimTimeboundActive",
    "Direct")
| extend ActorUpn      = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName)
| extend ActorObjectId = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id)
| extend ActorApp      = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName)
| extend ActorIp       = iff(isnotempty(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress)),
                             tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress),
                             tostring(InitiatedBy.app.ipAddress))
| extend Actor         = iff(isnotempty(ActorUpn), ActorUpn, ActorApp)
// The group: a target of type Group, or the Group.ObjectID / Group.DisplayName
// modified properties on the member's entry (Core Directory's shape), read
// from the serialized TargetResources so the order of entries does not matter.
| mv-apply tr = TargetResources on (
    summarize GroupIdFromTarget   = take_anyif(tostring(tr.id), tostring(tr.type) =~ "Group"),
              GroupNameFromTarget = take_anyif(tostring(tr.displayName), tostring(tr.type) =~ "Group"),
              MemberType          = take_anyif(tostring(tr.type), tostring(tr.type) in~ ("User", "ServicePrincipal", "Device")),
              MemberId            = take_anyif(tostring(tr.id), tostring(tr.type) in~ ("User", "ServicePrincipal", "Device")),
              MemberName          = take_anyif(iff(isnotempty(tostring(tr.userPrincipalName)), tostring(tr.userPrincipalName),
                                                   tostring(tr.displayName)), tostring(tr.type) in~ ("User", "ServicePrincipal", "Device"))
  )
| extend TargetsText = tostring(TargetResources)
| extend GroupIdFromProps   = extract(@'Group\.ObjectID"[^}]*?newValue[^0-9A-Fa-f}]*([0-9A-Fa-f-]{36})', 1, TargetsText)
| extend GroupNameFromProps = extract(@'Group\.DisplayName"[^}]*?newValue"\s*:\s*"(?:\\")?([^"\\]+)', 1, TargetsText)
| extend GroupId   = coalesce(GroupIdFromTarget, GroupIdFromProps)
| extend GroupName = coalesce(GroupNameFromTarget, GroupNameFromProps)
| extend IsBreakGlassGroup = GroupId in (BreakGlassGroupIds) or GroupName =~ "Break-Glass-Admins"
// By id when rendered; by name only on a standalone run (empty id list).
| extend IsAzurePimGroup = not(IsBreakGlassGroup) and (GroupId in (AzurePimGroupIds)
                           or (array_length(AzurePimGroupIds) == 0 and GroupName =~ "PIM-Azure-RG-Contributors"))
| extend AssignmentPath = iff(IsAzurePimGroup and AssignmentPath == "Direct", "AzurePimEligibleMember", AssignmentPath)
| where GroupId in (PrivilegedGroupIds) or IsBreakGlassGroup
     or GroupName in~ (PrivilegedGroupNames) or GroupName startswith "PIM-Tier"
| extend ActorSpId  = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.servicePrincipalId)
| extend ActorAppId = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.appId)
| extend IsIac = (isnotempty(ActorSpId) and ActorSpId in (IacPrincipalIds))
              or (isnotempty(ActorAppId) and ActorAppId in (IacPrincipalIds))
// The IaC name on an app that is NOT the IaC identity = someone impersonating
// the pipeline to look routine. Always High.
| extend IacNameSpoof = not(IsIac) and ActorApp =~ IacDisplayName
| extend Severity = case(
    IacNameSpoof,                          "High",
    IsBreakGlassGroup,                     "High",
    IsIac,                                 "Medium",
    AssignmentPath == "PimTimeboundActive", "Medium",
    AssignmentPath == "AzurePimEligibleMember", "Medium",
    "High")
| project TimeGenerated, Severity, AssignmentPath, GroupName, GroupId, IsBreakGlassGroup,
          MemberType, MemberName, MemberId, Actor, ActorUpn, ActorObjectId, ActorApp, ActorSpId,
          ActorIp, IsIac, IacNameSpoof, OperationName, CorrelationId
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
